/*
We have two trees on the same set of N vertices:
- red tree: Sigma moves only along red edges
- blue tree: Sugim moves only along blue edges

Sigma starts at X, Sugim at Y.
They move alternately, one edge per turn:
turn 1: Sigma
turn 2: Sugim
turn 3: Sigma
...

The game ends when after some turn both pieces are on the same vertex.

Let t be the number of turns when they first meet at vertex v.
Then:
- Sigma has moved ceil(t/2) times, so in the red tree:
    distR(X, v) = ceil(t/2)
- Sugim has moved floor(t/2) times, so in the blue tree:
    distB(Y, v) = floor(t/2)

Thus for some vertex v:
- either t = 2k, requiring distR(X,v)=k and distB(Y,v)=k
- or     t = 2k+1, requiring distR(X,v)=k+1 and distB(Y,v)=k

Equivalently:
t exists for v iff distR(X,v) == distB(Y,v) or distR(X,v) == distB(Y,v)+1
and then t = distR(X,v) + distB(Y,v).

We need the first meeting time, so take the minimum such t over all vertices.
If no such vertex exists, answer -1.

Since each color graph is a tree, distances from one source are found by one BFS/DFS each in O(N).
*/

public class Main {
    static class FastScanner {
        private final InputStream in;
        private final byte[] buffer = new byte[1 << 16];
        private int ptr = 0, len = 0;

        FastScanner(InputStream is) {
            in = is;
        }

        private int read() throws IOException {
            if (ptr >= len) {
                len = in.read(buffer);
                ptr = 0;
                if (len <= 0) return -1;
            }
            return buffer[ptr++];
        }

        int nextInt() throws IOException {
            int c;
            do {
                c = read();
            } while (c <= ' ' && c != -1);

            int sign = 1;
            if (c == '-') {
                sign = -1;
                c = read();
            }

            int val = 0;
            while (c > ' ') {
                val = val * 10 + (c - '0');
                c = read();
            }
            return val * sign;
        }
    }

    static int[] bfs(List<Integer>[] g, int start) {
        int n = g.length - 1;
        int[] dist = new int[n + 1];
        Arrays.fill(dist, -1);
        ArrayDeque<Integer> q = new ArrayDeque<>();
        dist[start] = 0;
        q.add(start);

        while (!q.isEmpty()) {
            int u = q.poll();
            for (int v : g[u]) {
                if (dist[v] == -1) {
                    dist[v] = dist[u] + 1;
                    q.add(v);
                }
            }
        }
        return dist;
    }

    public static void main(String[] args) throws Exception {
        FastScanner fs = new FastScanner(System.in);

        int N = fs.nextInt();
        int X = fs.nextInt();
        int Y = fs.nextInt();

        List<Integer>[] red = new ArrayList[N + 1];
        List<Integer>[] blue = new ArrayList[N + 1];
        for (int i = 1; i <= N; i++) {
            red[i] = new ArrayList<>();
            blue[i] = new ArrayList<>();
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < N - 1; i++) {
            int a = fs.nextInt();
            int b = fs.nextInt();
            red[a].add(b);
            red[b].add(a);
        }

        for (int i = 0; i < N - 1; i++) {
            int a = fs.nextInt();
            int b = fs.nextInt();
            blue[a].add(b);
            blue[b].add(a);
        }

        int[] distR = bfs(red, X);
        int[] distB = bfs(blue, Y);

        long ans = Long.MAX_VALUE;
        for (int v = 1; v <= N; v++) {
            int r = distR[v];
            int b = distB[v];
            if (r == b || r == b + 1) {
                ans = Math.min(ans, (long) r + b);
            }
        }

        System.out.println(ans == Long.MAX_VALUE ? -1 : ans);
    }
}

